{
    // FI_Standard_Order.ergo - the borrower's order for a fixed-interest (coupon) bond
    // Author: CannonQ (2026)
    //
    // ZC_Standard_Order with coupon and covenant terms in R4 and the longer bond R9 of
    // FI_Standard_Bond. The box holds the borrower's collateral and terms: a lender fills it into
    // a new bond, the borrower can cancel it, and anyone can refund it once it expires.
    // Use only with FI_Standard_Bond and ZC_Standard_BondVault. One order script serves ERG and
    // token repayment, fixed and on-close maturity: every term is in a register, so every open
    // FI order of this repayment asset sits at ONE address.
    //
    // CONSTANTS
    // CONST_BOND_HASH: Coll[Byte] - blake2b256 of the FI_Standard_Bond ErgoTree. The bond compiles
    //   in its vault, repayment token, coupon vault and covenant, so this hash also fixes the
    //   repayment asset: orders split into one address per repayment asset.
    // CONST_REPAYMENT_TOKEN: Coll[Byte] - that bond's repayment token, EMPTY for ERG. The deployer
    //   must compile it to match CONST_BOND_HASH; the script cannot read the bond's constant.
    // CONST_LIQUIDATION_HASH: Coll[Byte] - blake2b256 of the FI_Standard_Liquidation expression.
    //   A fill requires R7 to equal it. The deployer must take it from those exact bytes.
    //
    // ONE ASSET (as ZC)
    // A loan is lent and repaid in one asset, the repayment asset. A fill requires:
    //   ERG:   no principal tokens, principal R4(1) > 0, and floor R4(2) <= R4(0), so the floor
    //          never binds and the repayment is R4(0) nanoERG.
    //   token: principal tokens exactly ((repayment token, P > 0)), and at most 1000000 nanoERG
    //          in both R4(1) and R4(2): box minimums beside the token, never a second asset.
    // The bond takes its coupons in the same asset. Cancel and expiry ignore this rule.
    //
    // ORDER REGISTERS -> BOND REGISTERS (copied exactly; the lender cannot alter them)
    // R4: Coll[Long] -> bond R6: borrower values, length 15..64 to fill (7..64 to refund):
    //   0..6 as ZC: 0 repayment amount, 1 principal nanoERG, 2 repayment ERG floor, 3 maturity
    //     height (mode 0) or duration of at least 30 blocks (mode 1), 4 order expiry height,
    //     5 expiry fee >= 100000000 nanoERG, 6 maturity mode (0 fixed height, 1 on-close)
    //   7 coupon, raw units of the repayment asset: > 0 when 8 > 0, else >= 0
    //   8 coupon count, >= 0 (0 = no coupons)
    //   9 blocks from the start height to the first due height, 0..1000000000
    //   10 period between due heights, 1..1000000000
    //   11 grace after each due height, 0..1000000000, at most R4(10) when 8 > 0, and at least
    //     30 when 12 > 0
    //   12 minimum collateral ratio in bps, >= 0 (0 = no covenant; above 0 needs 8 >= 1, a fill
    //     guard in R8 and a first checkpoint the bond can record, see SCHEDULE)
    //   13 cure window in blocks, 30..1000000000 when 12 > 0 (see SCHEDULE)
    //   14 maximum oracle age in blocks, 1..100000 when 12 > 0
    //   15.. liquidation payload, not read here
    //   The ranges of 9, 10 and 11 are checked even with no coupons. They are the bond's clamps,
    //   so the bond reads these terms exactly as written.
    // R5: Coll[(Coll[Byte], Long)] -> bond R7: exact principal tokens: empty for ERG, or exactly
    //   one entry, the repayment token and the principal amount
    // R6: Coll[Byte] -> bond R5: blake2b256 of the borrower script
    // R7: Coll[Byte] -> bond R8: blake2b256 of the serialized liquidation expression; a fill
    //   requires it to equal CONST_LIQUIDATION_HASH, the standard FI_Standard_Liquidation
    // R8 (optional, not copied): Coll[Byte] - blake2b256 of a serialized fill guard expression.
    //   When present, a fill must also pass that expression, supplied in context var 1 and run
    //   with this order as SELF; it reads the new bond at OUTPUTS(1) and may read data inputs.
    //   FI_Standard_ERG_SigUSD_FillGuard is one: when R4(12) > 0 the bond must start with
    //   collateral worth at least that ratio of the repayment at a fresh oracle price. It has no
    //   margin: a bond filled at exactly its ratio can be recorded in breach at the next, lower
    //   oracle price, as early as the fill block, so the borrower pays the Record bounty and must
    //   cure; post collateral above the ratio for headroom. Absent, only an order with no
    //   covenant (R4(12) = 0) fills, and nothing about the collateral's value is checked.
    // Bond R4 = this order's id. Bond R9: Coll[Long], exactly 7 = (lender liquidation fee
    // reserve of at least 100000000 nanoERG, start height, maturity height, 0 coupons paid, -1 no
    // breach recorded, 0 no cure deadline, start height as the recollateralize clock).
    //
    // VALUE AND EXPIRY (as ZC)
    // Order value = collateral nanoERG + expiry fee; SELF.tokens are the collateral tokens.
    // Fill requires HEIGHT < R4(4) and returns the unused expiry fee with the principal.
    // Expiry refund requires HEIGHT >= R4(4): all tokens and >= value - fee go back to the borrower
    // at output var 0 (Int), tagged R4 = SELF.id, with no R5 and created at HEIGHT - 999 or later.
    // A borrower-script co-spend cancels at any height: another input whose script hashes to R6,
    // created fewer than 1051200 blocks before HEIGHT (an older box can be spent under storage
    // rent without its script running).
    //
    // FILL SHAPE (as ZC; no context vars, except var 1: Coll[Byte] the guard when R8 names one)
    // INPUTS(0) = SELF, so the bond asset id is this order's id and one order fills per
    // transaction.
    // Exactly 3 units are minted: 2 locked in the bond, 1 circulating.
    // OUTPUTS(0): the circulating unit at tokens(0), at any lender-chosen script (a wallet, an
    //   FI_Standard_LendOffer delivery...), created at HEIGHT - 999 or later. R4/R5: EIP-4
    //   name/description; R6: UTF-8 "0".
    // OUTPUTS(1): the bond. tokens(0) = (asset, 2), then SELF.tokens unchanged. Value at least
    //   collateral nanoERG + lender fee reserve bond R9(0), funded by the lender above the
    //   collateral, and at least 1000000 nanoERG beyond R9(0).
    // OUTPUTS(2): principal + expiry-fee refund, at the borrower script, R4 = SELF.id, no R5,
    //   created at HEIGHT - 999 or later. The tag keeps any other box paid to the borrower in the
    //   same transaction from counting as it.
    //
    // START AND MATURITY (as ZC)
    // Bond R9(1), the start height S, must lie in [HEIGHT - 8, HEIGHT]: a script cannot pin
    // HEIGHT exactly without making the transaction valid in a single block. The bond box's
    // creation height must equal it: the bond's Refresh reads the box's age from it.
    // Mode 0: maturity M = R4(3), at least HEIGHT + 30. Mode 1: M = S + R4(3), with R4(3) >= 30.
    // Either way M <= S + 788400 (about three years), the bond's maximum life. So a box stamped
    // at the start reaches the storage-rent age (1051200 blocks) no sooner than about 262800
    // blocks after maturity.
    //
    // SCHEDULE
    // Coupon k (from 0) falls due at S + R4(9) + k * R4(10); checkpoint k, where the bond can
    // record a covenant breach, is the same height. The coupon is missed, and an unpaid bond
    // liquidatable, from its due height plus the grace R4(11). With coupons (R4(8) > 0) a fill
    // requires:
    // - the first due height S + R4(9) at or after HEIGHT;
    // - the grace no longer than the period, R4(11) <= R4(10). Then at each checkpoint's due
    //   height every earlier coupon is paid or already missed, so with a grace of at least 3
    //   (every covenant order has 30 or more) the bond's coupon quiet zone (the last
    //   max(2, min(720, grace / 2)) blocks before the next unpaid coupon's miss, where it refuses
    //   Record breach) never covers a due height;
    // - the first coupon missed no earlier than HEIGHT + 30, so the bond is not liquidatable for
    //   a coupon until at least 30 blocks after the fill;
    // - the last coupon missed before M: last due + grace <= M - 1. A miss shuts repayment and
    //   opens liquidation, and M does both anyway, so a coupon missed only at or after M would
    //   change nothing.
    // With a covenant (R4(12) > 0) a fill also requires a guard in R8, a grace R4(11) of at
    // least 30, at least one coupon, and the first checkpoint's window closing before M - 720:
    // S + R4(9) + R4(11) + 720 < M. The bond records a breach only at HEIGHT in [checkpoint,
    // checkpoint + grace] with HEIGHT < M - 720, so a covenant with no such checkpoint could never
    // be tested. In on-close mode this reads R4(9) + R4(11) + 720 < R4(3).
    // A covenant also needs a cure window R4(13) of at least 30 blocks. A breach recorded at
    // HEIGHT h has its deadline from h + R4(13), and the bond refuses Cure and Repayment from the
    // deadline on, so the window must leave the borrower blocks in which to act.
    // With no coupons the covenant must be 0: the bond is a plain zero-coupon bond.
    //
    // STATE-BOX RULE (as ZC)
    // Supply is exactly 3 and 2 stay together for the asset's whole life: in the bond, then in
    // the vault. Genuineness of an asset X is a one-time check: the box with id X must have been
    // spent as an order with this exact script (and CONST_BOND_HASH), fewer than 1051200 blocks
    // after its creation height, because a box that old can be spent under storage rent without
    // its script running. FI_Standard_LendOffer makes that check, by this script's hash and the
    // box's age, before it buys an existing bond. The maximum life binds only bonds filled
    // through this script.
    //
    // ASSUMPTIONS
    // The liquidation expression is pinned by CONST_LIQUIDATION_HASH, and the covenant
    // expression is compiled into the bond, so CONST_BOND_HASH fixes it; this order only holds
    // the covenant's terms to the ranges above. The fill guard in R8 is the borrower's choice.
    //
    // BORROWER SCRIPTS
    // The borrower script must be one that only its owner can spend in every instance: P2PK,
    // multisig, or a contract whose keys are compiled-in constants. Anyone can create a box at a
    // script that reads its authority from its own registers, so naming one lets anyone cancel
    // this order and take everything it holds. The payouts here (principal, refund) carry only
    // the R4 tag, so whether the owner can spend them is up to that script.
    // FI_Standard_FractionalMint and FI_Standard_FractionalVault can be instantiated by anyone
    // and must never be the borrower hash. Builders should refuse any other kind of borrower
    // script.

    def numTokenInOutputs(tokenId: Coll[Byte]): Long = {
        OUTPUTS.fold(0L, { (a: Long, b: Box) =>
            val count = b.tokens.fold(0L, { (z: Long, t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) =>
                if (t._1 == tokenId) z + t._2 else z
            })
            a + count
        })
    }

    val borrowerHash = SELF.R6[Coll[Byte]].get
    val minted = numTokenInOutputs(SELF.id)

    if (minted > 0L) {
        // Fill
        val borrower = SELF.R4[Coll[Long]].get
        if (borrower.size < 15 || borrower.size > 64 || OUTPUTS.size < 3) {
            sigmaProp(false)
        } else {
            val lenderOut = OUTPUTS(0)
            val bond = OUTPUTS(1)
            val principal = OUTPUTS(2)
            val lender = bond.R9[Coll[Long]].get
            if (lender.size != 7) {
                sigmaProp(false)
            } else {
                val expiryFee = borrower(5)
                val mode = borrower(6)
                val collateralERG = SELF.value - expiryFee
                val fee = lender(0)
                val start = lender(1)
                val maturity = lender(2)
                val principalTokens = SELF.R5[Coll[(Coll[Byte], Long)]].get
                val decimals = fromBase16("30")

                // Lent and repaid in one asset, the repayment asset: the principal is that asset
                // alone, and the repayment needs nothing beside it but a box minimum. The empty
                // collection is taken from the box so the compiler cannot fold the constant.
                val noToken = SELF.id.slice(0, 0)
                val singleAsset = if (CONST_REPAYMENT_TOKEN == noToken) {
                    principalTokens.size == 0 && borrower(1) > 0L && borrower(2) <= borrower(0)
                } else {
                    principalTokens.size == 1 && principalTokens(0)._1 == CONST_REPAYMENT_TOKEN &&
                    principalTokens(0)._2 > 0L &&
                    borrower(1) <= 1000000L && borrower(2) <= 1000000L
                }

                val borrowerValid =
                    singleAsset &&
                    borrower(0) > 0L && borrower(1) >= 0L && borrower(2) > 0L &&
                    (mode == 0L || mode == 1L) &&
                    expiryFee >= 100000000L && expiryFee <= SELF.value - 1000000L &&
                    HEIGHT.toLong < borrower(4)

                val mintValid =
                    SELF.id == INPUTS(0).id && minted == 3L &&
                    lenderOut.creationInfo._1 > HEIGHT - 1000 &&
                    lenderOut.tokens.size > 0 &&
                    lenderOut.tokens(0)._1 == SELF.id && lenderOut.tokens(0)._2 == 1L &&
                    lenderOut.R4[Coll[Byte]].isDefined &&
                    lenderOut.R5[Coll[Byte]].isDefined &&
                    lenderOut.R6[Coll[Byte]].get == decimals

                val bondValid =
                    blake2b256(bond.propositionBytes) == CONST_BOND_HASH &&
                    bond.tokens.size > 0 &&
                    bond.tokens(0)._1 == SELF.id && bond.tokens(0)._2 == 2L &&
                    bond.tokens.slice(1, bond.tokens.size) == SELF.tokens &&
                    fee >= 100000000L && bond.value >= collateralERG && bond.value - collateralERG >= fee &&
                    bond.value - fee >= 1000000L &&
                    bond.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == SELF.id &&
                    bond.R5[Coll[Byte]].get == borrowerHash &&
                    bond.R6[Coll[Long]].get == borrower &&
                    bond.R7[Coll[(Coll[Byte], Long)]].get == principalTokens &&
                    bond.R8[Coll[Byte]].get == SELF.R7[Coll[Byte]].get &&
                    SELF.R7[Coll[Byte]].get == CONST_LIQUIDATION_HASH &&
                    // No coupon paid, no breach, no cure deadline; the recollateralize clock is
                    // the start.
                    lender.slice(3, 7) == Coll(0L, -1L, 0L, start)

                // The bond's creation height is its start: the bond's Refresh reads its age
                // from it.
                val startValid = start <= HEIGHT.toLong && start >= HEIGHT.toLong - 8L &&
                    bond.creationInfo._1.toLong == start
                val maturityValid = maturity <= start + 788400L && (
                    if (mode == 0L) maturity == borrower(3) && maturity >= HEIGHT.toLong + 30L
                    else borrower(3) >= 30L && maturity == start + borrower(3) && maturity > HEIGHT.toLong + 1L
                )

                // The coupon and covenant terms, each held to its range (R4 in the header).
                val coupon = borrower(7)
                val count = borrower(8)
                val firstOffset = borrower(9)
                val period = borrower(10)
                val grace = borrower(11)
                val ratio = borrower(12)
                val termsValid =
                    coupon >= 0L && count >= 0L && (count == 0L || coupon > 0L) &&
                    firstOffset >= 0L && firstOffset <= 1000000000L &&
                    period >= 1L && period <= 1000000000L &&
                    grace >= 0L && grace <= 1000000000L &&
                    ratio >= 0L && (ratio == 0L || (
                        borrower(11) >= 30L &&
                        borrower(13) >= 30L && borrower(13) <= 1000000000L &&
                        borrower(14) >= 1L && borrower(14) <= 100000L))
                // The SCHEDULE rules of the header: the first due height at or after the fill,
                // the grace no longer than the period, every coupon missed at least 30 blocks
                // after the fill and before maturity, and a covenant's first checkpoint window
                // closing before maturity - 720, where the bond shuts Record breach. The terms
                // are used raw; once termsValid holds they equal the bond's clamped reading.
                // The count test is
                // (count - 1) * period <= maturity - 1 - firstMissed, by integer division.
                val scheduleValid = termsValid && (count == 0L || {
                    val firstMissed = start + firstOffset + grace
                    start + firstOffset >= HEIGHT.toLong && grace <= period &&
                    firstMissed >= HEIGHT.toLong + 30L && firstMissed < maturity &&
                    count - 1L <= (maturity - 1L - firstMissed) / period
                }) && (ratio == 0L || (count >= 1L && start + firstOffset + grace + 720L < maturity))

                val principalPaid =
                    blake2b256(principal.propositionBytes) == borrowerHash &&
                    principal.creationInfo._1 > HEIGHT - 1000 &&
                    principal.value >= expiryFee && principal.value - expiryFee >= borrower(1) &&
                    principal.tokens == principalTokens &&
                    principal.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == SELF.id &&
                    principal.R5[Coll[Byte]].isDefined == false

                val core = borrowerValid && mintValid && bondValid && startValid && maturityValid &&
                    scheduleValid && principalPaid

                // The borrower's fill guard, when R8 names one. Var 1 only: var 0 is the
                // refund's Int.
                val guard = SELF.R8[Coll[Byte]]
                if (guard.isDefined) {
                    sigmaProp(core && blake2b256(getVar[Coll[Byte]](1).get) == guard.get) && executeFromVar[SigmaProp](1)
                } else {
                    sigmaProp(core && borrower(12) == 0L)
                }
            }
        }
    } else {
        // Cancel: an independent borrower-authorized co-spend, valid even for malformed R4
        // terms. R6 is read on every path, so a box without a readable R6 can never be spent.
        val borrowerAuth = INPUTS.exists { (b: Box) =>
            b.id != SELF.id && blake2b256(b.propositionBytes) == borrowerHash &&
            b.creationInfo._1 > HEIGHT - 1051200
        }
        if (borrowerAuth) {
            sigmaProp(true)
        } else {
            // Expiry refund, by anyone. Context var 0: Int refund output index.
            val borrower = SELF.R4[Coll[Long]].get
            val refundIndex = getVar[Int](0).get
            if (borrower.size < 7 || borrower.size > 64 || refundIndex < 0 || refundIndex >= OUTPUTS.size) {
                sigmaProp(false)
            } else {
                val fee = borrower(5)
                val refund = OUTPUTS(refundIndex)
                sigmaProp(
                    HEIGHT.toLong >= borrower(4) &&
                    fee >= 100000000L && fee <= SELF.value - 1000000L &&
                    blake2b256(refund.propositionBytes) == borrowerHash &&
                    refund.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == SELF.id &&
                    refund.creationInfo._1 > HEIGHT - 1000 &&
                    refund.R5[Coll[Byte]].isDefined == false &&
                    refund.value >= SELF.value - fee &&
                    refund.tokens == SELF.tokens
                )
            }
        }
    }
}
